# Seat 0 waits on 1s/4s with 1112344s 555z 789p. After drawing the
# winning 1s, seat 0 closes it instead of declaring tsumo. The structural
# waits remain 1s/4s, and 4s is still available. Replacement 7z is outside the wait.
# Seat 1 discards 4s. Declining a tsumo by a kan leaves no temporary furiten on
# either Mahjong Soul or Tenhou (real-log evidence: Tenhou 4 rons in 6 chances,
# Mahjong Soul 12 in 14), so seat 0 may ron on both rulesets.
# Winning sets: 234s, 44s, 555z, 789p and closed kan 1111s.
# Haku gives 1 han. Indicators 1z/2z point to absent 2z/3z (0 dora).
# No honba or sticks are paid.
# The 4s can finish 234s or the pair. For ron, the higher-paying pair
# reading adds 2 fu: 20 + 10 (menzen ron) + 32 (closed terminal kan) +
# 8 (closed honor triplet) + 2 (tanki) = 72 -> 80 fu.
# Base 80 * 2^(1+2) = 640; dealer ron rounds 6 * 640 = 3840 up to 3900.
# Dealer win repeats East 1 at honba 1.

[meta]
name: declined_tsumo_outside_riichi
title: Declining a tsumo by a kan leaves no temporary furiten on either client
rules: both
source: engine.md §4.2, rules.md §5.13, docs/notes/p3-closeout.md

[round]
scores: 25000 25000 25000 25000

